<h2 id="ha-ctrl-009-acceptance">Acceptance and evidence</h2>

1. Make an unsaved draft, undo a change, save one successfully and have one save rejected. Record what draft is actually kept and how it differs from the saved configuration.
2. Move around nested conditions and actions, and move and delete blocks, using the native keyboard routes. Check that focus and execution order hold. Record any limit you cannot fix.
3. Review an action-only test and a real triggered trace separately. In a controlled environment, confirm which branches and targets each one evaluates.
4. Test a disabled, an enabled, a running and a deleted automation, plus a concurrent edit and a lost connection. These documentation examples must not save or run anything.

Record the Home Assistant version, the browser, the fixture or device, the starting state, the expected and observed results, and where the evidence is kept. A documentation check is not a live-device test.

For the wording of saved, enabled and running see [States, requests and errors](../content/writing-guidelines/states-and-errors.html). For the fields an editor is built from see [Schema selectors and configuration forms](schema-selectors.html).

